.TH CTE 1 "September 2026" "CTE 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cte \- Tablić card game engine, tournament arena, and interactive player
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cte
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cte
(C Tablić Engine) is an implementation of the classic Balkan fishing card game
.B Tablić
(Tablanet). It features bitboard SWAR move generation, configurable AI strategies (random, dumb, greedy, minimax/cheater),
championship tournaments (Round Robin and Knockout Cup), persistent player profiles with Elo rating tracking,
and an interactive ncurses TUI interface.
.PP
When launched without arguments on an interactive terminal (TTY),
.B cte
automatically opens the full-screen interactive TUI main menu.

.SH RULES OF TABLIĆ
Tablić is played with a standard 52-card French deck.
.SS Game Objective
Be the first player or team to reach the target winning score (usually 101 points, or 51 points for quick matches).
.SS Card Values
.IP \(bu 2
Cards
.B 2
through
.B 10
have their pip face value (2 to 10).
.IP \(bu 2
.B Ace
counts as either 1 or 11, chosen to the player's advantage.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Jack
counts as 12.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Queen
counts as 13.
.IP \(bu 2
.B King
counts as 14.
.SS Gameplay & Captures
At each turn, a player must play exactly one card from their hand:
.IP \(bu 2
.B Capture:
If the card played matches the value of a card on the table, or matches the sum of two or more cards on the table,
the player captures those cards along with the played card.
Crucially, multiple distinct combinations may be captured in a single turn if each combination sums to the played card.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Drop (Trailing):
If no capture is made (or if the player chooses not to capture), the card remains face up on the table.
.SS Tablić Bonus
If a player's capture clears the table completely, leaving zero cards, the player scores a
.B Tablić
worth
.B +1 bonus point
immediately.
.SS End of Round Scoring
When all 52 cards have been played, the player who made the last capture collects any remaining cards on the table.
Points are then tallied:
.IP \(bu 2
.B Majority of Cards:
The player or team with the strictly greatest number of cards won (at least 27 cards) receives
.B +3 points
(split 1.5/1.5 if tied).
.IP \(bu 2
.B High Cards:
Each Ace, King, Queen, Jack, and 10 is worth
.B 1 point.
.IP \(bu 2
.B 10 of Diamonds:
Worth
.B 2 points
("two-points ten").
.IP \(bu 2
.B 2 of Clubs:
Worth
.B 1 point
("two-points two").
.PP
There are 25 base card points in each deck, plus any Tablić points scored during the round.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-players " \fInumber\fR"
Number of players: 2 (default), 3, or 4 (up to 16 in tournament mode).
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-team
Enable 4-player 2v2 team mode (valid only with \fB\-n 4\fR).
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-ai-type " \fIlist\fR"
AI strategy or comma-separated list of strategies for bots.
Supported values:
.BR random " (uniform pseudo-random moves),"
.BR dumb " (picks lowest value capture or drop),"
.BR greedy " (evaluates immediate points and card count),"
.BR cheater " or " minimax " (tactical lookahead)."
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " \fImode\fR"
UI frontend mode:
.BR cli " (standard terminal I/O, default),"
.BR tui " (ncurses interactive screen)."
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-style " \fIstyle\fR"
Card display style:
.BR unicode " (default, e.g. [A♠], [10♥]),"
.BR ascii " (e.g. [AS], [10H])."
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-game " \fImode\fR"
Game match mode:
.BR h-vs-ai " (Human vs AI, default),"
.BR h-vs-h " (Human vs Human),"
.BR ai-vs-ai " (AI vs AI simulation)."
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-winning-score " \fIpoints\fR"
Target match score required to win (default: 101).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-rounds " \fInumber\fR"
Maximum number of deck cycles/rounds to play (default: 0 = unlimited, until target score).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-seed " \fInumber\fR"
Seed for the pseudo-random number generator (default: current system epoch).
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-tournament " \fItype\fR"
Run a tournament directly:
.BR round-robin " (all participants play each other),"
.BR cup " or " knockout " (single-elimination tournament bracket)."
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-profile " \fIname\fR"
Active player profile name for persistent statistics and Elo rating updates.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-leaderboard
Display the stored player Elo leaderboard and exit immediately.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display the command-line usage summary and exit.

.SH TOURNAMENT ARENA
CTE includes a complete tournament engine capable of managing 2 to 16 participants:
.TP
.B Round Robin
Every participant plays a match against every other participant. Final standings are ranked by match wins,
lowest losses, total points scored, and total Tablićs.
.TP
.B Knockout Cup
A single-elimination tournament bracket for powers of 2 (2, 4, 8, 16 participants). Sudden-death rounds are
played if any match concludes in a tie, ensuring a decisive tournament champion.

.SH PROFILES AND ELO RATING
Player performance is tracked across games and tournaments:
.IP \(bu 2
Initial Elo rating is set to
.B 1200.
.IP \(bu 2
Rating updates follow the standard logistic Elo formula with
.B K = 32.
.IP \(bu 2
Profiles record total matches played, wins, losses, ties, total Tablićs, and points.
.IP \(bu 2
Storage is atomic via POSIX temporary file writes and renaming to prevent data corruption.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/cte/profiles.dat
User profile and Elo database. Defaults to
.I ~/.local/share/cte/profiles.dat
if
.B $XDG_DATA_HOME
is unset.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B cte
Launch the full interactive ncurses TUI menu.
.TP
.B cte \-g h-vs-ai \-a greedy \-w 51
Play a quick 2-player match against the Greedy AI to 51 points.
.TP
.B cte \-n 4 \-t \-a greedy,cheater,greedy
Play a 4-player 2v2 team match.
.TP
.B cte \-T round-robin \-n 4 \-w 25
Simulate a 4-bot Round Robin tournament to 25 points and display the standings table.
.TP
.B cte \-T cup \-n 8 \-p "Grandmaster"
Participate in an 8-player Knockout Cup tracked under profile "Grandmaster".
.TP
.B cte \-\-leaderboard
Print the current player Elo leaderboard.

